title The card that shipped its markers
prompt Continue the same Diffuser lap through its send.
think The send's first rebase surfaced a nested conflict marker in construction/ITINERARY.md, and a nested marker inside a conflict body is a shape no honest merge writes, so I read upstream directly rather than assuming my own resolution had gone wrong.
think Upstream's card carried three literal marker lines. Reds first, and I was already holding that exact region, so the repair rode the commit I was landing.
think Before writing the row I asked whether a guard existed, expecting none -- and one does, correct and rostered at tier lap, reading 18,069 files and gating markers at zero.
think That turned the finding from a missing guard into a misplaced one, which is a better red: the roster runs cold at the open and hot at the close, and the marker was made by the send's final rebase, which sits after both.
think The same sentence is already written in derived-spine for %681, and the repair it names -- the pre-push hook, a placement rather than a new instrument -- asks one scan and no other. A second class has now asked for the same seat.
obs THE RED IS BOOKED AS %731, fetched from the anointed spine before booking. The ledger census was republished 730 to 731 in the same commit, since reds_ledger_monotone refuses a headline disagreeing with its own measured spine.
obs THE MARKERS STOOD FOR TWO COMMITS on the anointed remote before the repair, in the one page every ship reads whole at every lap.
obs THE SEND TOOK FOUR REBASES and every one conflicted on the same two lines -- the card's Git nib. Eight ships rewriting one literal on every lap is a guaranteed conflict rather than an unlucky one, and it is the reason a rebase is where a marker gets written.
obs I DID NOT BUILD THE PLACEMENT. Extending the hook means extending its control and witness, which is its own bounded lap; it is claimed and pushed instead, so a peer reading the new row does not reach for it twice.
loom send rebases=4 conflicts=4 conflicted_lines=2 remotes_pushed=2
loom conflict_marker files_scanned=18069 marker_lines=0 marked_files=0 seated_tier=lap
loom reds spine_next_free=731 census_before=730 census_after=731
rota lap 4931, row 1 -- Air, the row that feels; the boundary it felt was the send seam, where a guard green on every ship still ships a broken page.
file construction/REDS.md books %731 and republishes the census the spine measures
file construction/ITINERARY.md repairs the three marker lines and carries the nib forward
file construction/fleet-claims.kyri closes the landed locality claim and opens the placement claim
scope close a red found mid-send, book it against the anointed spine, claim the repair rather than take it
status GREEN before send -- conflict_marker reads zero on metal, reds_ledger_monotone green, both remotes carry the work
recommend keep-going -- the placement lap is claimed and bounded; the two-lane question on the card still wants Keaton's word
